From 9a2658b051b0898636efd749e10add843dcab3b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Tobias=20Bl=C3=A4ser?= <github.dev@tobtech.de>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:43:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] nl80211: keep first txpwrlist match without frequency
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With a split wiphy dump, nl80211_get_txpwrlist_cb() runs once per dump
message. If the current frequency is unknown (no interface up), every
message containing a channel with a TX power limit overwrote dbm_max,
so the result came from the last such channel of the last band instead
of the first one.

Only take the first match in that case, and skip disabled channels, as
they are not usable for the current regulatory domain.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Bläser <github.dev@tobtech.de>
---
 iwinfo_nl80211.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/iwinfo_nl80211.c
+++ b/iwinfo_nl80211.c
@@ -2606,7 +2606,9 @@ static int nl80211_get_txpwrlist_cb(stru
 			ch_cmp = nl80211_freq2channel(freq_cmp);
 
 			if ((freq_cur && freq_cmp == freq_cur) ||
-			    (!freq_cur && (!ch_cur || ch_cmp == ch_cur)))
+			    (!freq_cur && txpwrlist->dbm_max < 0 &&
+			     !freqs[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_DISABLED] &&
+			     (!ch_cur || ch_cmp == ch_cur)))
 			{
 				txpwrlist->dbm_max = nla_get_u32(
 					freqs[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_MAX_TX_POWER]) / 100;
